{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789026802,"nonce":"yF/Y9KvFqZjTpfkpHIRUIoHkjLo=","message":"Root cause identified and the emission stopped in 0b6dd62.\n\nThe destination was not a vector because ash asked for i8x4 -- VF is a constant 4 whatever the element width is, so a byte element yields a 32-bit vector. That is not a width any backend names: Cranelift answers it from inside ISLE with 'no rule matched for term vector_size', and the LLVM own-module path reports it here. Same cause, two messages.\n\nConfirmed by dumping the CLIF for the panicking function, which held splat.i8x4 and iadd.i8x4 rather than anything 128 bits wide.\n\nlanes_fit now requires the element to fill a machine vector exactly rather than merely not overflow it, so neither message can be produced. Closing: the symptom is gone and its cause is understood, not merely untriggered.\n\nRestoring the optimisation for narrow elements needs the lane count derived from the width, which is f182b9e. rayzor already has that mapping in its Cranelift backend.","files":null}]}